NAME
    rssh - start a managed shell with the rsudo shell extension

SYNOPSIS
    rssh [<shell-argument> ...]

DESCRIPTION
    rssh starts the managed shell environment with rsudo.lib.sh selected as the
    shell extension.

    Before delegating to shell, rssh exports m_SHELL_EXT as the current
    rsudo.lib.sh path and installs an RSSH prompt in PS1. The prompt uses tput
    capabilities for terminal styling and shows the current user, host and
    working directory.

    All command-line arguments are forwarded unchanged to shell.

ENVIRONMENT
    m_SHELL_EXT
        Exported as $m_LIB_DIR/sys/sh/rsudo/rsudo.lib.sh before shell startup.

    PS1
        Replaced with the RSSH prompt used by the managed shell session.

    SHELL
        Consumed by shell to select the shell executable. See the shell manual.

EXIT STATUS
    rssh delegates shell preparation, execution and resulting status to shell.
    A non-zero status indicates failure to prepare or start the managed shell.

DEPENDENCIES
    rssh is an m-integrated command. It uses the m runtime roots and delegates
    to the shell facility. The selected shell session loads rsudo.lib.sh through
    m_SHELL_EXT.

SEE ALSO
    shell
    rsudo
    rsudo.lib.sh
